gst-plugins-rs-webrtc for Debian/Ubuntu
=======================================

Why this package ships prebuilt shared objects
----------------------------------------------

The upstream Rust workspace (gst-plugins-rs) declares `rust-version = 1.92`.
The newest rustc in the Ubuntu archive is 1.75 (noble), so Launchpad's
builders cannot compile it from source. Rather than not exist, this package
carries the shared objects compiled by the project's GitHub Actions pipeline,
on native amd64 and arm64 runners, from the upstream tag named in the version.

Verifying the binaries
----------------------

Every build is published as a GitHub release with a `SHA256SUMS` file:

    https://github.com/goabonga/gst-plugins-rs-rpi/releases

The `.so` files installed by this package are byte-identical to the ones in
`gst-plugins-rs-webrtc-<version>-<arch>.tar.gz` of the matching release, and
the workflow that produced them is public:

    https://github.com/goabonga/gst-plugins-rs-rpi/actions/workflows/release.yml

Series support
--------------

Packages are built for the Ubuntu series whose libraries the plugins were
linked against (noble, matching the GitHub Actions runners). Installing them
on an older series will fail on library symbol versions.

 -- Chris <goabonga@pm.me>
